Package: x13cpp
Title: Seasonal Adjustment with the X13cpp Engine
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Chris", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "cyg5005@gmail.com"))
Description: An R interface to X13cpp, a from-scratch C++17 port of the U.S.
    Census Bureau's X-13ARIMA-SEATS seasonal adjustment program. The package
    provides a 'seasonal_adjust()' entry point returning a structured result
    object with accessor functions for diagnostics, forecasts, and save
    tables, plus example economic time series bundled for experimentation.
    No output files are ever written automatically; call 'write_outputs()'
    explicitly to persist results to disk. The underlying C++ estimation
    engine is still under development (see the parent repository), so the
    computational path currently stubs out with an informative error;
    this package establishes the public API and data bundling ahead of
    that wiring.
